(@user_oleksandr_derkach, @clinic_id, NULL, 'google_maps',
    'places/ChIJn5PmYSPrTRMR1bfj5M6l8J8/reviews/Ci9DQUlRQUNvZENodHljRjlvT25GVFFVTmtUMlZQZUd0VE9FSXpibEl3ZEZaWmExRRAB',
    1, 'en', 'I’ve been to many countries but such disgusting medicine I meet for the first time. In urgency I had to spend around 5 hours with trombus risk after 8 hours flight and they took all the locals who came after me in front of me just because they speak Serbian. As for orthopedy they don’t take you even with uput/ insurance, whatever. I tried it for five times. Private medicine is more expensive than in EU even though an average salary 1000€ across Montenegro. Try not to get sick in this country because it’s easier to die than to get a medicine help 💀',
    NULL, NULL, 'I’ve been to many countries but such disgusting medicine I meet for the first time. In urgency I had to spend around 5 hours with trombus risk after 8 hours flight and they took all the locals who came after me in front of me just because they speak Serbian. As for orthopedy they don’t take you even with uput/ insurance, whatever. I tried it for five times. Private medicine is more expensive than in EU even though an average salary 1000€ across Montenegro. Try not to get sick in this country because it’s easier to die than to get a medicine help 💀', NULL, NULL, NULL,
    0, '2026-09-29 00:00:00'),

(@user_goran_mars, @clinic_id, NULL, 'google_maps',
    'places/ChIJn5PmYSPrTRMR1bfj5M6l8J8/reviews/Ci9DQUlRQUNvZENodHljRjlvT25GSmVtTTNORTFvZUROc1dIYzRjRnAxV1ZvNFRIYxAB',
    1, 'bs', 'Baš su užasni sestru imam sa posebnim potrebama mora da uzme nova sočiva niko se na tel ne javlja kada smo bili rekli su da ce se javiti sramota su',
    'Baš su užasni sestru imam sa posebnim potrebama mora da uzme nova sočiva niko se na tel ne javlja kada smo bili rekli su da ce se javiti sramota su', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL,
    0, '2026-09-29 00:00:00'),

(@user_ariel, @clinic_id, NULL, 'google_maps',
    'places/ChIJn5PmYSPrTRMR1bfj5M6l8J8/reviews/Ci9DQUlRQUNvZENodHljRjlvT214QmVGcEpjVU0xVkRCeVlWZFVabUZhZEVsbk4wRRAB',
    5, 'en', '⭐⭐⭐⭐⭐
Review for the maternity department the public hospital, Clinical Center of Montenegro🤰🏽: As a family that has experienced both private hospitals Podgorica has to offer, our unequivocal recommendation is to skip them and choose the public hospital instead.
Our experiences in the private sector were unacceptable: During our first birth, the doctor needed to go on vacation, so he rushed us into an unnecessary emergency C-section even though there was no fetal distress. During our second birth at the newer private hospital, the professor promised us the entire way that she would let us try for a natural birth—but a week before the delivery, she changed her attitude, became rude, refused to let us try, and terrified us extremely (showing us graphic pictures of mothers with uterine ruptures without any medical logic).

Fortunately, since we come from a medical background and practiced it in our country of origin, we immediately understood there was no reason to be intimidated by her manipulations and refused to give in to the pressure. We decided to take action and turn to the public hospital.

At the public hospital, we found the complete opposite: a human, pleasant, and attentive medical staff. Despite language barriers with the nurses who didn\'t speak English, everyone showed endless patience, and a dedicated doctor accompanied my wife and provided her with perfect care. We successfully achieved a natural birth! My wife and the baby are feeling great and are completely healthy, without needing another C-section.

The physical conditions in the ward might be a bit outdated and lacking in resources (less clean, etc.), but that is entirely secondary to the main point: the right to give birth naturally and safely, without succumbing to foreign considerations and pressures from doctors in the private sector. Thank you very much',
    NULL, NULL, '⭐⭐⭐⭐⭐
Review for the maternity department the public hospital, Clinical Center of Montenegro🤰🏽: As a family that has experienced both private hospitals Podgorica has to offer, our unequivocal recommendation is to skip them and choose the public hospital instead.
Our experiences in the private sector were unacceptable: During our first birth, the doctor needed to go on vacation, so he rushed us into an unnecessary emergency C-section even though there was no fetal distress. During our second birth at the newer private hospital, the professor promised us the entire way that she would let us try for a natural birth—but a week before the delivery, she changed her attitude, became rude, refused to let us try, and terrified us extremely (showing us graphic pictures of mothers with uterine ruptures without any medical logic).

Fortunately, since we come from a medical background and practiced it in our country of origin, we immediately understood there was no reason to be intimidated by her manipulations and refused to give in to the pressure. We decided to take action and turn to the public hospital.

At the public hospital, we found the complete opposite: a human, pleasant, and attentive medical staff. Despite language barriers with the nurses who didn\'t speak English, everyone showed endless patience, and a dedicated doctor accompanied my wife and provided her with perfect care. We successfully achieved a natural birth! My wife and the baby are feeling great and are completely healthy, without needing another C-section.

The physical conditions in the ward might be a bit outdated and lacking in resources (less clean, etc.), but that is entirely secondary to the main point: the right to give birth naturally and safely, without succumbing to foreign considerations and pressures from doctors in the private sector. Thank you very much', NULL, NULL, NULL,
    0, '2026-09-29 00:00:00'),

(@user_alina_vikto, @clinic_id, NULL, 'google_maps',
    'places/ChIJn5PmYSPrTRMR1bfj5M6l8J8/reviews/Ci9DQUlRQUNvZENodHljRjlvT214ZllXNTBaakV0YlZkdWNISkVjRFpsV2twM1NrRRAB',
    5, 'ru', 'Хочу оставить отзыв конкретно о Гематологическом дневном отделении. Выразить огромную благодарность всему персоналу, медсестрам , докторам, проходим постановку диагноза и сейчас уже лечение лимфомы моей мамы у докторов Иванны Микитич и Йованы Шабан, таких сердечных, граммонтных и приятных докторов надо еще поискать! Мои самые большие благодарности. Весь персонал в отделении очень приятный, отзывчивый, всегда посодействует что бы помочь, очень верю, что диагноз моей мамы победим через пару курсов здесь! Благодарю Вас за Ваш труд!',
