(@user_vladimir_yanyshevsky, @clinic_id, NULL, 'google_maps',
    'places/ChIJM8Gt42Q2TBMRvLuBwVtNCEQ/reviews/Ci9DQUlRQUNvZENodHljRjlvT25sSGRFdGtTRzE1YW1WRWJqUjNXbFYzUmw4M2NYYxAB',
    1, 'en', 'The worst hospital I\'ve ever been in. I was there for seven days with a fracture, and now I have to spend another two weeks in another hospital to correct the "work" of these doctors. Specifically, the surgeon, Dr. Dino, and the hospital director. These incompetent people didn\'t correct the bone displacement and applied an external fixator to a bone with a huge displacement. They didn\'t give me a tetanus shot, even though they were required to do so by all the rules. They allowed the wound area to become infected. The infection caused my temperature to rise above 39 degrees , but the orderly insisted it was just the fracture. In seven days with an open fracture, they only dressed the wound twice (which caused dirt to accumulate and the infection to develop). For an entire floor of patients, only one staff member remained at night, and he was always smoking somewhere and it was impossible to reach him. Just think about it: they discharged me with a catheter in my vein that had been inserted seven days earlier and sent me to the airport. Even the nurse at the airport was shocked when she removed it. I really hope the Montenegrin Ministry of Health will pay attention to this horror happening there. I wish everyone a speedy recovery and I don\'t recommend anyone end up in this "hospital." They\'re more likely to cripple you than cure you. By the way, I\'m currently being treated at another hospital for this blood poisoning, and they charged me €2,500. Good luck to everyone!',
    NULL, NULL, 'The worst hospital I\'ve ever been in. I was there for seven days with a fracture, and now I have to spend another two weeks in another hospital to correct the "work" of these doctors. Specifically, the surgeon, Dr. Dino, and the hospital director. These incompetent people didn\'t correct the bone displacement and applied an external fixator to a bone with a huge displacement. They didn\'t give me a tetanus shot, even though they were required to do so by all the rules. They allowed the wound area to become infected. The infection caused my temperature to rise above 39 degrees , but the orderly insisted it was just the fracture. In seven days with an open fracture, they only dressed the wound twice (which caused dirt to accumulate and the infection to develop). For an entire floor of patients, only one staff member remained at night, and he was always smoking somewhere and it was impossible to reach him. Just think about it: they discharged me with a catheter in my vein that had been inserted seven days earlier and sent me to the airport. Even the nurse at the airport was shocked when she removed it. I really hope the Montenegrin Ministry of Health will pay attention to this horror happening there. I wish everyone a speedy recovery and I don\'t recommend anyone end up in this "hospital." They\'re more likely to cripple you than cure you. By the way, I\'m currently being treated at another hospital for this blood poisoning, and they charged me €2,500. Good luck to everyone!', NULL, NULL, NULL,
    3, '2026-06-29 00:00:00'),

